sions based on these numbers. Here's what our calculators use for the 2026 tax year:\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ul\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"2026 Federal income tax brackets (10% through 37%)\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"2026 Standard deductions by filing status\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"FICA rates: Social Security (6.2%) + Medicare (1.45%)\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"2026 Social Security wage cap: $184,500\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Additional Medicare Tax: 0.9% above $200,000\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"State-specific tax rates and exemptions for IL, TX, FL, CA, NY\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"2026 401(k) contribution limits ($24,500 + catch-up)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs mt-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"That said, our tools produce estimates. We can't account for every possible deduction, credit, or special circumstance in your life. If you're making a major financial decision, talk to a CPA — our calculators are a starting point, not the final word.\\\"}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"29:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"id\\\":\\\"contact\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-12 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-8 text-center\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"svg\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"xmlns\\\":\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\",\\\"width\\\":24,\\\"height\\\":24,\\\"viewBox\\\":\\\"0 0 24 24\\\",\\\"fill\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"stroke\\\":\\\"currentColor\\\",\\\"strokeWidth\\\":2,\\\"strokeLinecap\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"strokeLinejoin\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"lucide lucide-mail h-8 w-8 text-emerald-400 mx-auto mb-4\\\",\\\"aria-hidden\\\":\\\"true\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"path\\\